---
name: C# Patterns
description: C# 12+ idioms, nullable reference types, record types, primary constructors, and .NET 10 patterns for this project.
alwaysApply: true
---

## Language version: C# 12 / .NET 10

### File structure

- ✅ File-scoped namespaces: `namespace My.Namespace;`
- ✅ Explicit `using` directives — no implicit usings in Domain/Application
- ❌ Never `using static` in domain or application layers

### Null safety

- ✅ Nullable reference types enabled (`<Nullable>enable</Nullable>`) — treat all warnings as errors
- ✅ Use `string?` for optional strings; never `string` + null check after the fact
- ✅ Prefer `is null` / `is not null` over `== null` / `!= null`
- ✅ Use null-coalescing throw: `value ?? throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(value))`
- ❌ Never suppress nullable warnings with `!` without a comment explaining why

### Records

- ✅ Output DTOs: `public sealed record UserOutput(Guid Id, string Name);`
- ✅ Commands and queries: `public sealed record RegisterUserCommand(...) : ICommand<UserOutput>;`
- ✅ Domain events: `public sealed record UserRegisteredEvent(Guid UserId) : IDomainEvent;`
- ❌ Never use `record` for domain entities — use `class` with private setters

### Primary constructors (C# 12)

- ✅ Use for services/handlers with simple DI: `public class MyHandler(IMyRepo repo, IUnitOfWork uow)`
- ❌ Avoid for domain entities — explicit private constructor + static `Create(...)` factory required

### Collections

- ✅ `IReadOnlyList<T>` for output collections — never expose `List<T>` from domain
- ✅ Collection expressions: `List<string> items = [item1, item2];`
- ✅ `[..existingList, newItem]` for spread
- ✅ `Enumerable.Empty<T>()` or `[]` for empty collections — never `new List<T>()`

### Pattern matching

- ✅ Switch expressions over switch statements for mapping
- ✅ `is { Property: value }` property patterns in guards
- ❌ Never use `as` + null check — use `is T typed` pattern instead

### Async

- ✅ All async methods return `Task<T>` or `ValueTask<T>` — never `async void`
- ✅ `ConfigureAwait(false)` in library/infrastructure code
- ✅ `CancellationToken` as last parameter on all async public methods
- ❌ Never `.Result` or `.Wait()` — always `await`

### String handling

- ✅ Raw string literals for multi-line: `"""..."""`
- ✅ Interpolated strings for dynamic: `$"User {id} not found"`
- ❌ Never string interpolation in Serilog templates — use structured `{Property}` syntax
- ❌ Never `string.Format` — use interpolation

### LINQ

- ✅ Method syntax over query syntax
- ✅ `FirstOrDefaultAsync` + null check — never `SingleOrDefault` in queries (use `FirstOrDefault` unless uniqueness is enforced at DB level)
- ❌ Never `Count() > 0` — use `Any()`
- ❌ Never `Where(...).FirstOrDefault()` — use `FirstOrDefault(predicate)`
